Now, Lulu, that's a real man.

269
00:16:14,857 --> 00:16:16,097
Just look at that mustache!

270
00:16:16,857 --> 00:16:17,237
Whatever!

271
00:16:17,617 --> 00:16:19,637
Nobody's manlier than Tile Stone!

272
00:16:19,637 --> 00:16:21,997
Hey, mister!

273
00:16:22,697 --> 00:16:22,957
Hmm?

274
00:16:23,297 --> 00:16:24,657
What's this crowd about?

275
00:16:25,057 --> 00:16:27,437
Oh, it was just some boneheaded pirates

276
00:16:27,437 --> 00:16:29,457
trying to pick a fight with the shipwrights again.

277
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,077
You know, happens all the time.

278
00:16:32,237 --> 00:16:34,497
But our guys send them packing like always.

279
00:16:34,857 --> 00:16:36,637
Those pirates will never learn their lesson.

280
00:16:37,277 --> 00:16:38,337
Whoa, that's nuts!

281
00:16:38,597 --> 00:16:40,297
The shipwrights can beat up pirates?

282
00:16:40,577 --> 00:16:42,377
Ah, you must be tourists, huh?

283
00:16:42,597 --> 00:16:43,757
The shipwrights are well.

284
00:16:44,137 --> 00:16:44,317
Hmm.

285
00:16:44,617 --> 00:16:46,217
They're like celebrities to us.

286
00:16:46,617 --> 00:16:49,277
In fact, you might say that this crowd is their fan club.

287
00:16:49,517 --> 00:16:51,557
We're always watching the Galley Lock Company.

288
00:16:52,437 --> 00:16:54,837
They're strong, they're skilled,

289
00:16:55,337 --> 00:16:58,697
and they're the pride of every citizen in Water 7.

290
00:17:07,817 --> 00:17:08,337
Wow!

291
00:17:08,677 --> 00:17:10,057
I can't wait to meet them!

292
00:17:10,057 --> 00:17:11,937
Hey, Luffy!

293
00:17:13,997 --> 00:17:16,277
Let's hurry up and get the gold traded in, okay?

294
00:17:16,617 --> 00:17:18,497
This is fun, but it can wait till later.

295
00:17:18,617 --> 00:17:18,997
Come on!

296
00:17:18,997 --> 00:17:20,397
I just...

297
00:17:20,397 --> 00:17:35,277
It says that we're in the Backstreet Shopping District.

298
00:17:35,537 --> 00:17:38,097
Seems awfully crowded for a Backstreet, if you ask me.

299
00:17:38,097 --> 00:17:42,017
Kind of neat that they have places to walk around, though.

300
00:17:42,397 --> 00:17:45,137
They must have put a lot of thought into the town's design.

301
00:17:45,277 --> 00:17:45,597
Yeah.

302
00:17:49,437 --> 00:17:49,837
Scary!

303
00:17:49,837 --> 00:17:53,097
Would you look at that?

304
00:17:53,097 --> 00:17:54,597
What a beautiful woman!

305
00:17:54,597 --> 00:17:55,977
She's gorgeous!

306
00:17:55,977 --> 00:17:58,277
A real once-in-a-lifetime beauty!

307
00:17:58,277 --> 00:18:01,437
Ugh, this place is full of Sanji's.

308
00:18:01,437 --> 00:18:05,657
What is that guy selling?

309
00:18:05,657 --> 00:18:08,037
What is that guy selling?

310
00:18:08,037 --> 00:18:08,957
It looks creepy.

311
00:18:08,957 --> 00:18:11,037
It's just a mask shop.

312
00:18:11,037 --> 00:18:16,657
I noticed a lot of people around town wearing them, so they must buy them from there.

313
00:18:16,657 --> 00:18:17,677
It's something you wear?

314
00:18:17,677 --> 00:18:19,077
I thought that was their face.

315
00:18:19,077 --> 00:18:20,537
Wow, that's a big relief.

316
00:18:23,877 --> 00:18:29,597
It seems the people here take the sea train to San Faldo Island, where they hold a costume carnival every day.

317
00:18:29,997 --> 00:18:30,337
Huh?

318
00:18:30,497 --> 00:18:31,477
How do you know that?

319
00:18:31,537 --> 00:18:32,437
We just got here.

320
00:18:32,677 --> 00:18:34,997
The people walking by are talking about it.

321
00:18:35,517 --> 00:18:35,917
Whoa.

322
00:18:36,577 --> 00:18:37,997
And do you hear everything they say?

323
00:18:37,997 --> 00:18:40,077
I can't help it.

324
00:18:41,457 --> 00:18:46,497
Ever since I was young, I've made it a habit to keep a critical eye and ear on my environment.

325
00:18:47,217 --> 00:18:47,777
Oh.

326
00:18:48,597 --> 00:18:49,517
Wow, Robin.

327
00:18:49,877 --> 00:18:50,817
That's cool.

328
00:18:56,037 --> 00:18:56,517
Huh.

329
00:18:57,077 --> 00:18:57,637
Doctor.

330
00:18:58,317 --> 00:18:58,537
Hmm?

331
00:18:59,377 --> 00:19:00,097
See that?

332
00:19:00,497 --> 00:19:01,817
I think we found your bookstore.

333
00:19:01,917 --> 00:19:02,437
Really?

334
00:19:03,477 --> 00:19:05,517
Can we go inside now?

335
00:19:06,517 --> 00:19:07,397
Of course.

336
00:19:07,397 --> 00:19:08,277
Be my guest.

337
00:19:08,777 --> 00:19:10,557
Today is the best day ever!

338
00:19:22,557 --> 00:19:24,917
CP-9.

339
00:19:24,917 --> 00:19:25,917
Hey!

340
00:19:42,297 --> 00:19:43,717
What are you waiting for?

341
00:19:43,717 --> 00:19:43,917
Hey!

342
00:19:43,917 --> 00:19:45,857
What are you waiting for?

343
00:19:45,857 --> 00:20:15,237
If I'm in my human form, maybe it'll be okay.

344
00:20:15,237 --> 00:20:16,237
Huh?

345
00:20:16,237 --> 00:20:16,697
Huh?

346
00:20:16,697 --> 00:20:17,197
Huh?

347
00:20:17,197 --> 00:20:17,777
Why?

348
00:20:18,457 --> 00:20:19,877
What a funny mask!

349
00:20:20,077 --> 00:20:20,957
What's your costume?

350
00:20:21,737 --> 00:20:22,117
Oh!

351
00:20:22,817 --> 00:20:23,377
Uh...

352
00:20:23,377 --> 00:20:24,557
A human...

353
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:24,917
Reindeer?

354
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:25,837
Hmm!

355
00:20:25,837 --> 00:20:27,197
Ha ha ha ha ha!

356
00:20:27,397 --> 00:20:29,097
Well, as long as you're having fun, right?

357
00:20:29,397 --> 00:20:30,397
Ha ha ha ha!

358
00:20:30,617 --> 00:20:30,897
Hmm.

359
00:20:31,717 --> 00:20:32,237
Oh...

360
00:20:32,237 --> 00:20:32,877
Hey, wait.

361
00:20:39,277 --> 00:20:39,817
Robin?

362
00:20:39,817 --> 00:20:40,057
Robin?

363
00:20:47,417 --> 00:20:48,197
Hello?

364
00:20:48,197 --> 00:20:48,457
Robin?

365
00:20:48,457 --> 00:21:01,117
Robin?

366
00:21:01,117 --> 00:21:24,857
Pity, I was hoping that we could kill you in your sleep.

367
00:21:24,857 --> 00:21:32,737
You bastards sure got a lot of nerve. Who are you?

368
00:21:54,857 --> 00:21:55,117
Thank you.

369
00:21:55,117 --> 00:21:55,637
Thank you.

370
00:23:06,084 --> 00:23:10,364
First on the next, One Piece, The Frankie Family and Iceberg.

371
00:23:10,364 --> 00:23:12,424
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

